    skos:altLabel "Tutu (Vocabulary, 1911)"@en ;
    skos:definition "The twentieth address of chapter 125 in the Papyrus of Ani. Budge renders the name doubly wicked. The god is addressed as coming forth from Ati, and the address is bound to one denial: I have not defiled the wife of a man."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
